 "notes": [
  "General Guidelines\n- All technical courses taken in satisfaction of major requirements must be taken for a letter grade.\n- No more than one upper division course may be used to simultaneously fulfill requirements for a student’s major and minor programs.\n- A minimum overall grade point average (GPA) of 2.0 is required for all work undertaken at UC Berkeley.\n- A minimum GPA of 2.0 is required for all technical courses taken in satisfaction of major requirements.\n- Students must complete a minimum of 48 engineering units. See concentrations for recommendations.\n- Students must complete a minimum of 36 units of upper division Technical Topics courses.\n- Students must complete a minimum of 24 units of upper division Bioengineering courses, including at least two Bioengineering Fundamentals courses, one Bioengineering Design Project or Research course, and one Bioengineering Lab course.\nFor a detailed plan of study by year and semester, please see the Plan of Study tab."
